CLI-INIT-01 Before any question, `callisto init` prints `Detected:` with the ecosystems, the origin remote URL, and each package's qualified id, version, last tag, and executable names for executable-producing packages. Artifact selection includes only supported Cargo binary targets. 

CLI-INIT-09 init exits 1 without writing when callisto.toml already exists (unless `--workflow` is given, which then writes only the workflow and leaves callisto.toml as it is) or when the directory is not inside a Git repository, each with a help line naming the fix. With no `origin` remote configured, or one that is not a hosted remote (such as a local path or `file://` URL), init instead writes callisto.toml, skips the workflow and shipping-binaries questions, and emits an `init-origin-missing` warning diagnostic that never shows the `origin` value; `--workflow` or `--artifact-target` without a hosted `origin` exits 1 naming the fix, and `callisto release` refuses later. 

CLI-INIT-10 With a non-terminal stdin and no --yes, init exits 2 with `E240` naming --yes and every other missing flag; with --yes it exits 2 with `E241` naming each missing flag: --product-package when --artifact-target is given and more than one supported Cargo package produces a binary. 

CLI-INIT-12 init exits without writing: 2 for an empty or repeated target triple (`E196`), a --product-package that is absent or not a supported Cargo binary producer (`E189`), or --product-package given without --artifact-target (`E298`); 1 for --artifact-target when no supported Cargo package produces a binary (`E188`), and for shipping binaries, by flag or by answer, when `origin` is not a GitHub repository (`E198`). An npm `bin` or Python `[project.scripts]` product selected for an artifact fails with a typed unsupported-builder diagnostic; registry-only npm and PyPI releases remain valid. 

